IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hca-dates`
IMPORT `hca-rules`

-- Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) -- the questions of the GENERAL HEALTH SERVICE PROVIDER: a person who provides a health
-- service that is not the practice of a health profession registered under the National Law (an unregistered
-- practitioner, or a registered one working outside their profession). The second seat, beside the complainant's in
-- hca-seat.l4: the Act puts the code of conduct, the Commissioner's notices and the prohibition orders on this person.
-- Every rule it uses is in hca-rules.l4, shared with the complainant's seat, so the two seats cannot disagree about the
-- law; the names here are its own.
--
-- The Commissioner's beliefs and satisfaction are inputs; the provider's duties with deadlines (ss 35, 39, 41, 52, 58) are
-- DEONTIC rules run inside, from hca-rules.l4.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Health
-- Complaints Act 2016, Version No. 011 (22 October 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published
-- with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance
-- with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Health Complaints Act 2016 -- the general health service provider`

§§ `Am I covered`

@export Do I provide a "general health service", so that the general code of conduct and the Commissioner's prohibition orders apply to me (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) s 3)? A general health service is a health service that is not the practice of a health profession registered under the National Law; a registered practitioner working outside their profession provides one too.
GIVEN `what kind of service do I provide` IS A `Kind of service` @desc The kind of service: an activity meant or claimed to assess, maintain or improve health or to diagnose, prevent or treat illness, injury or disability; disability, palliative or aged care; surgery; prescribing or dispensing a drug or a therapeutic aid; health education; therapeutic counselling or psychotherapy; a support service for one of these; an ancillary service; a prescribed service; or none of these
      `does my ancillary service affect patients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an ancillary service only: whether it affects or may affect people receiving health services
      `is it the practice of my registered profession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service is the practice of a health profession under the National Law in which you are registered (answer no if you are unregistered, or the service is outside your profession)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Do I provide a general health service` MEANS
    `s 3 -- a general health service` (`s 3 -- a health service` `what kind of service do I provide` `does my ancillary service affect patients`) `is it the practice of my registered profession`

§§ `The general code of conduct, as the provider`

@export Does my practice break the general code of conduct on safe and ethical practice, consent, informed choice or reporting other providers (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) Schedule 2 clauses 1 to 4)?
GIVEN `is it a general health service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provide the service as a general health service (not the practice of your registered profession)
      `is my practice unsafe or unethical` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are not providing the service in a safe and ethical manner
      `do I lack competence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have not maintained the necessary competence in your field
      `is it outside my training or qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service is outside your experience or training, or one you are not qualified to provide
      `did I recommend something not needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you prescribed or recommended treatments or appliances that did not serve the client's needs
      `did I fail to refer on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not refer a client to another competent provider when that was appropriate
      `did I fail to suggest another opinion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not recommend additional opinions or services when appropriate
      `did I fail to help find other care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not help a client find other appropriate care when required and practicable
      `did I fail to encourage telling their doctor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not encourage the client to tell their treating doctor about your treatment
      `did I fail to warn of interactions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not advise the client of possible adverse interactions with other treatments you knew or should have known of
      `was I culturally insensitive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not provide the service in a culturally sensitive way
      `did I get proper consent first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before starting, you made sure appropriate consent complying with Victorian law was obtained
      `did I not accept informed choices` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not accept the client's right to make informed choices
      `did I try to talk a client out of medical treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you tried to dissuade a client from seeking or continuing medical treatment
      `did I not co-operate with other providers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not communicate and co-operate with other providers in the client's best interests
      `do I believe another provider puts clients at serious risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the course of treatment or care, you formed the reasonable belief that another health service provider has placed or is placing clients at serious risk of harm
      `did I refer that to the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you referred the matter to the Health Complaints Commissioner
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my practice break the code on safe practice` MEANS
    `the code answer` `is it a general health service` (`as an answer` (
           `cl 1 -- contravened` (`Clause 1 facts` WITH
                `the service was not provided in a safe and ethical manner` IS `is my practice unsafe or unethical`
                `the provider lacked the necessary competence` IS `do I lack competence`
                `the service was outside the provider's experience, training or qualifications` IS `is it outside my training or qualifications`
                `the provider prescribed or recommended something not serving the client's needs` IS `did I recommend something not needed`
                `the provider did not refer on when that was appropriate` IS `did I fail to refer on`
                `the provider did not recommend another opinion when appropriate` IS `did I fail to suggest another opinion`
                `the provider did not help find other services when required and practicable` IS `did I fail to help find other care`
                `the provider did not encourage telling the treating doctor` IS `did I fail to encourage telling their doctor`
                `the provider did not advise of possible adverse interactions it knew or should have known of` IS `did I fail to warn of interactions`
                `the service was not culturally sensitive` IS `was I culturally insensitive`)
        OR `cl 2 -- contravened` `did I get proper consent first`
        OR `cl 3 -- contravened` `did I not accept informed choices` `did I try to talk a client out of medical treatment` `did I not co-operate with other providers`
        OR `cl 4 -- contravened` `do I believe another provider puts clients at serious risk` `did I refer that to the Commissioner`))

@export Does my practice break the general code of conduct on adverse events, infection control, or practising while ill, impaired, medicated or under the influence (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) Schedule 2 clauses 5, 6, 7, 10 and 11)?
GIVEN `is it a general health service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provide the service as a general health service
      `did an adverse event occur` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an adverse event occurred in the course of your treatment or care
      `did I not act promptly to limit harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not take appropriate and timely measures to minimise harm
      `is there no first aid available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether appropriate first aid is not available in your practice
      `was it serious and I got no emergency help` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a serious adverse event occurred and you did not obtain emergency assistance
      `did I not tell the client or not fix the cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not promptly disclose the event to the client, or took no remedial steps against it recurring
      `did I not report it where appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not report it to the relevant authority where that was appropriate
      `have I not adopted infection precautions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have not adopted standard precautions for infection control
      `does my skin penetration break Victorian law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your skin penetration or invasive procedures do not comply with Victorian law
      `do I have a transmissible condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been diagnosed with a medical condition that can be passed on to clients
      `do I practise in a way that risks passing it on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you practise in a way that puts clients at risk
      `have I not followed a registered practitioner's advice on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have not taken and followed advice from a suitably qualified registered practitioner on changing your practice
      `do I treat under the influence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have treated clients under the influence of alcohol or unlawful substances
      `do I take prescribed medication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are taking prescribed medication
      `have I not got advice on its effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have not obtained advice from the prescriber or dispensing pharmacist on its effect on your ability to practise
      `have I treated while it may impair me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you treated clients where your capacity was or may have been impaired
      `have I treated with an impairment risking harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you treated clients while suffering an impairment, condition or addiction that places or is likely to place them at risk of harm
      `do I have an impairment that could risk clients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a mental or physical impairment that could place clients at risk
      `have I not sought advice on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have not sought advice from a suitably qualified health practitioner on modifying or stopping your practice
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my practice break the code on events and health` MEANS
    `the code answer` `is it a general health service` (`as an answer` (
           `cl 5 -- contravened` (`Clause 5 facts` WITH
                `an adverse event occurred` IS `did an adverse event occur`
                `the provider did not take appropriate and timely measures to minimise harm` IS `did I not act promptly to limit harm`
                `appropriate first aid was not available` IS `is there no first aid available`
                `the event was serious and emergency help was not obtained` IS `was it serious and I got no emergency help`
                `the event was not promptly disclosed to the client, or no remedial steps were taken` IS `did I not tell the client or not fix the cause`
                `it was not reported to the relevant authority where appropriate` IS `did I not report it where appropriate`)
        OR `cl 6 -- contravened` `have I not adopted infection precautions` `does my skin penetration break Victorian law`
        OR `cl 7, 10, 11 -- contravened` (`Provider's health facts` WITH
                `the provider has a transmissible condition` IS `do I have a transmissible condition`
                `the provider practised in a way that put clients at risk of it` IS `do I practise in a way that risks passing it on`
                `the provider did not take and follow a registered practitioner's advice on it` IS `have I not followed a registered practitioner's advice on it`
                `the provider treated clients under the influence of alcohol or unlawful substances` IS `do I treat under the influence`
                `the provider takes prescribed medication` IS `do I take prescribed medication`
                `the provider did not get advice on its effect` IS `have I not got advice on its effect`
                `the provider treated clients while capacity was or may have been impaired by it` IS `have I treated while it may impair me`
                `the provider treated clients with an impairment likely to place them at risk of harm` IS `have I treated with an impairment risking harm`
                `the provider has an impairment that could place clients at risk` IS `do I have an impairment that could risk clients`
                `the provider did not seek advice on it` IS `have I not sought advice on it`)))

@export Does my practice break the general code of conduct on claims to cure cancer, unsupported claims, or misinformation about my services or qualifications (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) Schedule 2 clauses 8 and 9)?
GIVEN `is it a general health service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provide the service as a general health service
      `have I claimed I can cure cancer or a terminal illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have claimed or represented that you are qualified, able or willing to cure cancer or another terminal illness
      `have I claimed to treat cancer symptoms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim to be able to treat or relieve symptoms of cancer or another terminal illness
      `can I substantiate it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you can substantiate that claim
      `have I misinformed clients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have misinformed or misrepresented your products, services, qualifications, training or affiliations
      `have I used a qualification to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have used a qualification to mislead clients or the public about your competence
      `have I made unprovable claims of effectiveness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have claimed, directly or in advertising, that a treatment works when that cannot be substantiated
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my practice break the code on claims` MEANS
    `the code answer` `is it a general health service` (`as an answer` (`cl 8, 9 -- contravened` (`Claims facts` WITH
        `the provider claimed to be able or willing to cure cancer or a terminal illness` IS `have I claimed I can cure cancer or a terminal illness`
        `the provider claimed to treat or relieve symptoms of cancer or a terminal illness` IS `have I claimed to treat cancer symptoms`
        `the provider can substantiate that claim` IS `can I substantiate it`
        `the provider misinformed about products, services, qualifications or affiliations` IS `have I misinformed clients`
        `the provider used a qualification to mislead about competence` IS `have I used a qualification to mislead`
        `the provider made efficacy claims it cannot substantiate` IS `have I made unprovable claims of effectiveness`)))

@export Does my practice break the general code of conduct on money or sexual conduct with clients (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) Schedule 2 clauses 12 and 13)?
GIVEN `is it a general health service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provide the service as a general health service
      `have I financially exploited a client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have financially exploited a client
      `have I given services not meant to help health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provided services or treatments not designed to maintain or improve the client's health or wellbeing
      `have I taken or offered referral inducements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted or offered financial inducements or gifts in referral arrangements
      `have I asked a client for money or gifts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked a client to give, lend or bequeath money or gifts that benefit you directly or indirectly
      `have I behaved sexually or too personally with a client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you engaged in behaviour of a sexual or close personal nature with a client
      `have I had a sexual or inappropriate relationship with a client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you engaged in a sexual or other inappropriate close personal, physical or emotional relationship with a client
      `did I start a relationship with a former client too soon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you began a sexual relationship with a former client before a reasonable time had passed since the therapeutic relationship ended
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my practice break the code on money and conduct` MEANS
    `the code answer` `is it a general health service` (`cl 12, 13 -- contravened` (`Money and conduct facts` WITH
        `the provider financially exploited the client` IS `have I financially exploited a client`
        `the provider gave services not designed to maintain or improve health or wellbeing` IS `have I given services not meant to help health`
        `the provider accepted or offered referral inducements or gifts` IS `have I taken or offered referral inducements`
        `the provider asked the client to give, lend or bequeath money or gifts` IS `have I asked a client for money or gifts`
        `the provider engaged in sexual or close personal behaviour with a client` IS `have I behaved sexually or too personally with a client`
        `the provider had a sexual or inappropriate close relationship with a client` IS `have I had a sexual or inappropriate relationship with a client`
        `the provider began a sexual relationship with a former client too soon` IS `did I start a relationship with a former client too soon`))

@export Does my practice break the general code of conduct on privacy, records, insurance, or giving clients the code and complaint information (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) Schedule 2 clauses 14 to 17)?
GIVEN `is it a general health service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provide the service as a general health service
      `have I broken privacy law on health information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have not complied with the privacy laws on clients' health information (Health Records Act 2001, Privacy and Data Protection Act 2014, Privacy Act 1988)
      `are my records not properly kept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do not keep accurate, legible, up-to-date and secure clinical records for each consultation
      `did a client ask to see their records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a client asked for access to information in their health records
      `did I not help them see them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you did not take the steps needed to give access
      `did a client or their lawyer ask for a transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a client or their legal representative asked for their health record to be transferred
      `did I not transfer it in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you did not help transfer it in a timely way
      `do I lack indemnity insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do not have appropriate indemnity insurance for your practice
      `do I not make the code and complaint information available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do not bring to clients' attention, or make easily available, a copy of the code of conduct and information on how to complain to the Commissioner
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my practice break the code on records and information` MEANS
    `the code answer` `is it a general health service` (`cl 14 to 17 -- contravened` (`Records and information facts` WITH
        `the provider broke a privacy law on the client's health information` IS `have I broken privacy law on health information`
        `the provider did not keep accurate, legible, up-to-date and secure records` IS `are my records not properly kept`
        `the client asked for access to their records` IS `did a client ask to see their records`
        `the provider did not help with that access` IS `did I not help them see them`
        `the client or their lawyer asked for the records to be transferred` IS `did a client or their lawyer ask for a transfer`
        `the provider did not help transfer them in a timely way` IS `did I not transfer it in time`
        `the provider has no appropriate indemnity insurance` IS `do I lack indemnity insurance`
        `the provider did not make the code and the complaints information easily available` IS `do I not make the code and complaint information available`))

§§ `What the Commissioner may require of me, and by when`

-- The situation arises only when a complaint about you is with the Commissioner.
@export Have I done what the Commissioner required in time (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) ss 35, 39, 41, 52 and 58)? A written response to the complaint's issues (s 35), documents in a conciliation (s 41), a report on an undertaking (s 39), or a written response to an investigation or follow up report (ss 52, 58), each by the last day the notice, requirement or report set (as extended under s 36 or 42). Late is an offence, unless (ss 39, 52, 58) you have a reasonable excuse.
GIVEN `what was required` IS A `Provider's act` @desc What the Commissioner required: a written response to each issue (s 35), a report on implementing an undertaking (s 39), documents or evidence in a conciliation (s 41), a written response to an investigation report (s 52), or to a follow up report (s 58)
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice or requirement was given, or the report was received
      `the last day allowed` IS A DATE @desc The last day the notice, requirement or report allows (as extended by the Commissioner, if it was)
      `have I done it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have done it
      `the day I did it` IS A DATE @desc The day you did it (any date if you have not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today
      `do I have a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a reasonable excuse (for example that it would incriminate you, or breach legal privilege: ss 77, 78); it counts only for ss 39, 52 and 58, whose offences say "without reasonable excuse"
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Have I done what the Commissioner required in time` MEANS
    `what became of it, by dates` `what was required` `the day of the notice` `the last day allowed` `have I done it` `the day I did it` `today` `do I have a reasonable excuse`

-- s 35(2), s 41(2): the time "must be no more than 20 business days after the notice is given"; s 39(2): "must not be more
-- than 12 months after the undertaking is given". Over the limit: JUST FALSE. ss 52, 58 set no limit: NOTHING-kind *silent*.
@export Is the time the Commissioner set me within the Act's limit (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) ss 35(2), 39(2) and 41(2))? A written response or documents: no more than 20 business days after the notice; a report on an undertaking: no later than 12 months after the undertaking.
GIVEN `what was required` IS A `Provider's act` @desc What the Commissioner required (s 35, 39, 41, 52 or 58)
      `business days the notice allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc For s 35 or 41: the number of business days after the notice was given that the notice allowed
      `the day I gave the undertaking` IS A DATE @desc For s 39: the day you gave the undertaking (any date otherwise)
      `the day fixed for my report` IS A DATE @desc For s 39: the day the Commissioner fixed for your report (any date otherwise)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the time set within the Act's limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what was required`
    WHEN `give the Commissioner a written response to each issue (s 35)` THEN `as an answer` (`business days the notice allowed` AT MOST 20)
    WHEN `produce the documents or evidence (s 41)` THEN `as an answer` (`business days the notice allowed` AT MOST 20)
    WHEN `report on implementing the undertaking (s 39)` THEN `as an answer` (NOT (`the day fixed for my report` `is after` (`the date` 12 `months after` `the day I gave the undertaking`)))
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 82(1) "The Commissioner may publish a statement setting out the name of a health service provider if the health
-- service provider has failed to provide a written response under section 58 in the time required in a follow up report
-- under section 56(2)(c)." s 83(1), (2): "Before publishing a follow up statement, the Commissioner must give the health
-- service provider a reasonable opportunity to make ... submissions" and written notice of it. Not failed: JUST FALSE
-- ("if"). No opportunity given yet: JUST FALSE ("before", read as a condition, fork F9).
@export Can the Commissioner publish my name for not responding to a follow up report (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) ss 82 and 83)? Only if you failed to give the written response in the time the follow up report required, and only after giving you written notice and a reasonable opportunity to make submissions.
GIVEN `did I fail to respond to the follow up report in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to give the written response to a follow up report within the time it set (s 58)
      `was I given notice and a chance to make submissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner gave you written notice and a reasonable opportunity to make oral or written submissions on the proposed statement
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my name be published for not responding` MEANS
    `as an answer` (`did I fail to respond to the follow up report in time` AND `was I given notice and a chance to make submissions`)

§§ `Warning statements and prohibition orders`

-- These arise only when the Commissioner is investigating you, or you have been convicted of a prescribed offence or are
-- under a Disability Service Safeguards Act 2018 order.
-- s 87 "(1) The Commissioner may publish a statement setting out the name of a general health service provider if the
-- Commissioner has commenced an investigation under Part 4 and the Commissioner reasonably believes that -- (a) the
-- general health service provider has contravened a code of conduct ...; and (b) it is necessary to publish the statement
-- to avoid an imminent and serious risk to -- (i) the life, health, safety or welfare of a person; or (ii) the health,
-- safety or welfare of the public. (2) ... (a) if -- (i) the general health service provider has been convicted or found
-- guilty of a prescribed offence; or (ii) after completing an investigation under Part 4, the Commissioner is satisfied
-- that the general health service provider has contravened a code of conduct ...; and (b) the Commissioner reasonably
-- believes that it is necessary ... to avoid a serious risk". "If": unmet, JUST FALSE.
@export Can the Commissioner publish a warning statement naming me (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) s 87)? During an investigation, if the Commissioner reasonably believes you breached the code and a warning is needed to avoid an imminent and serious risk; or after a prescribed conviction or a completed investigation finding a breach, if needed to avoid a serious risk.
GIVEN `has an investigation of me begun` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has commenced an investigation under Part 4 into your service
      `has the investigation been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that investigation has been completed
      `does the Commissioner believe I breached the code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the investigation: whether the Commissioner reasonably believes you contravened a code of conduct applying to your service
      `is the Commissioner satisfied I breached the code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After completing the investigation: whether the Commissioner is satisfied you contravened a code of conduct
      `have I been convicted of a prescribed offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of an offence prescribed by the regulations (not deposited here)
      `does the Commissioner believe it is needed to avoid an imminent serious risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner reasonably believes publishing is necessary to avoid an imminent and serious risk to a person's life, health, safety or welfare or to the public
      `does the Commissioner believe it is needed to avoid a serious risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner reasonably believes publishing is necessary to avoid a serious risk (answer yes if the risk is also imminent)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can a warning statement name me` MEANS
    `as an answer` (
           (`has an investigation of me begun` AND `does the Commissioner believe I breached the code` AND `does the Commissioner believe it is needed to avoid an imminent serious risk`)
        OR ((`have I been convicted of a prescribed offence` OR (`has an investigation of me begun` AND `has the investigation been completed` AND `is the Commissioner satisfied I breached the code`)) AND `does the Commissioner believe it is needed to avoid a serious risk`))

-- Interim prohibition orders. s 90(1): "If the Commissioner is, in an investigation under Part 4, investigating whether or
-- not a code of conduct applying to a general health service has been contravened, the Commissioner may make an order --
-- (a) prohibiting ... for up to 12 weeks; or (b) imposing ... conditions ... for up to 12 weeks." (1A): an order for up to
-- 12 weeks against "a person who is subject to a prohibition order or interim prohibition order made under the Disability
-- Service Safeguards Act 2018" if a copy was given to the Commissioner. s 91(1): "must not make an interim prohibition order
-- in relation to a general health service provider -- (a) unless -- (i) the Commissioner reasonably believes that the
-- general health service provider has contravened a code of conduct ...; or (ii) ... has been convicted or found guilty of
-- a prescribed offence; or (iii) ... is subject to a [DSSA order]; and (b) unless the Commissioner is satisfied that it is
-- necessary to make the order to avoid a serious risk". (2): for (1A), the serious risk alone. s 91A: for (1A), the
-- Commissioner "must give a written notice of the proposed order" and "must invite ... a written or verbal submission"
-- (fork F10: not done, JUST FALSE). "Must not ... unless": unmet, JUST FALSE.
@export Can the Commissioner make an interim prohibition order against me, banning or putting conditions on my service for up to 12 weeks (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) ss 90, 91 and 91A)? During an investigation of a possible code breach, if the Commissioner reasonably believes you breached the code (or you have a prescribed conviction or a disability safeguards order) and is satisfied the order is needed to avoid a serious risk; or, after notice and a chance to respond, if you are under a disability safeguards order.
GIVEN `is the Commissioner investigating a possible code breach by me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is, in a Part 4 investigation, investigating whether you contravened a code of conduct applying to your general health service
      `does the Commissioner believe I breached the code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner reasonably believes you contravened a code of conduct
      `have I been convicted of a prescribed offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of an offence prescribed by the regulations
      `am I under a disability safeguards order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are subject to a prohibition order or interim prohibition order under the Disability Service Safeguards Act 2018
      `was a copy of that order given to the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether a copy was given to the Commissioner under s 130(2)(b) or 132(2)(b) of that Act
      `was I given notice and invited to respond` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an order based on the disability safeguards order alone: whether the Commissioner gave you written notice of the proposed order and invited a written or verbal submission within a reasonable time
      `is the Commissioner satisfied it is needed to avoid a serious risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied the order is necessary to avoid a serious risk to a person's life, health, safety or welfare, or to the public
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can an interim prohibition order be made against me` MEANS
    `as an answer` (`under s 90(1)` OR `under s 90(1A)`)
    WHERE
        `under s 90(1)` MEANS
                `is the Commissioner investigating a possible code breach by me`
            AND (`does the Commissioner believe I breached the code` OR `have I been convicted of a prescribed offence` OR `am I under a disability safeguards order`)
            AND `is the Commissioner satisfied it is needed to avoid a serious risk`
        `under s 90(1A)` MEANS
                `am I under a disability safeguards order`
            AND `was a copy of that order given to the Commissioner`
            AND `was I given notice and invited to respond`
            AND `is the Commissioner satisfied it is needed to avoid a serious risk`

-- s 90(1) "for up to 12 weeks"; (3) "An order under this section takes effect on the service of the order". The last day
-- it can run is taken as the day 12 weeks (84 days) after the day of service (fork F11).
@export Until when can an interim prohibition order against me run at most (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) s 90)? Up to 12 weeks from when it was served on you; it may be revoked earlier (s 94).
GIVEN `the day it was served on me` IS A DATE @desc The day the interim prohibition order was served on you
GIVETH A DATE
`When does the interim order end at the latest` MEANS
    `the date` 84 `days after` `the day it was served on me`

-- s 95(1): after "an investigation under Part 4 into a possible contravention by a general health service provider of a
-- code of conduct", an order prohibiting or imposing conditions "permanently or for the period specified". (1A): against a
-- person under a DSSA order whose copy was given. s 96(1) "must not make a prohibition order ... (a) unless -- (i) the
-- Commissioner is satisfied that the general health service provider has contravened a code of conduct ...; or (ii)
-- convicted ... of a prescribed offence; or (iii) ... subject to a [DSSA order]; and (b) unless ... satisfied that it is
-- necessary ... to avoid a serious risk". (2) for (1A). s 95A: notice and invitation for (1A) (fork F10).
@export Can the Commissioner make a prohibition order against me, banning or putting conditions on my service permanently or for a set period (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) ss 95, 95A and 96)? After investigating a possible code breach, if the Commissioner is satisfied you breached the code (or you have a prescribed conviction or a disability safeguards order) and that the order is needed to avoid a serious risk; or, after notice and a chance to respond, if you are under a disability safeguards order.
GIVEN `has the Commissioner investigated a possible code breach by me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has conducted a Part 4 investigation into a possible contravention by you of a code of conduct
      `is the Commissioner satisfied I breached the code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied you contravened a code of conduct
      `have I been convicted of a prescribed offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of an offence prescribed by the regulations
      `am I under a disability safeguards order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are subject to a prohibition order or interim prohibition order under the Disability Service Safeguards Act 2018
      `was a copy of that order given to the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether a copy was given to the Commissioner under s 130(2)(b) or 132(2)(b) of that Act
      `was I given notice and invited to respond` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an order based on the disability safeguards order alone: whether the Commissioner gave you written notice of the proposed order and invited a submission
      `is the Commissioner satisfied it is needed to avoid a serious risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied the order is necessary to avoid a serious risk to a person's life, health, safety or welfare, or to the public
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can a prohibition order be made against me` MEANS
    `as an answer` (`under s 95(1)` OR `under s 95(1A)`)
    WHERE
        `under s 95(1)` MEANS
                `has the Commissioner investigated a possible code breach by me`
            AND (`is the Commissioner satisfied I breached the code` OR `have I been convicted of a prescribed offence` OR `am I under a disability safeguards order`)
            AND `is the Commissioner satisfied it is needed to avoid a serious risk`
        `under s 95(1A)` MEANS
                `am I under a disability safeguards order`
            AND `was a copy of that order given to the Commissioner`
            AND `was I given notice and invited to respond`
            AND `is the Commissioner satisfied it is needed to avoid a serious risk`

-- s 101 "(1) A person on whom the Commissioner has imposed an interim prohibition order or a prohibition order may apply
-- to VCAT for a review of the Commissioner's decision to impose the order. (2) An application for review under subsection
-- (1) must be made within 28 days after the later of -- (a) the day on which the order is served on the person; or (b) if,
-- under the [VCAT Act], the person requests a statement of reasons for the decision, the day on which the statement of
-- reasons is given to the person or the person is informed under section 46(5) of that Act that a statement of reasons will
-- not be given." The last day is 28 days after the later day; while reasons are requested but not yet given or refused,
-- the period has not begun to run on (b), and the answer uses the day of service as the floor (fork F12).
GIVEN `the day it was served on me`       IS A DATE
      `did I ask for a statement of reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `have I been given reasons or told none will come` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the reasons or refusal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 101(2) -- the last day` `the day it was served on me` `did I ask for a statement of reasons` `have I been given reasons or told none will come` `the day of the reasons or refusal` MEANS
    `the date` 28 `days after` `the later day`
    WHERE
        `the later day` MEANS
            IF `did I ask for a statement of reasons` AND `have I been given reasons or told none will come` AND (`the day of the reasons or refusal` `is after` `the day it was served on me`)
            THEN `the day of the reasons or refusal`
            ELSE `the day it was served on me`

@export By when must I apply to VCAT to review an interim prohibition order or prohibition order made against me (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) s 101)? Within 28 days after the later of the day it was served and, if you asked for a statement of reasons, the day you were given the reasons or told none would be given.
GIVEN `the day it was served on me` IS A DATE @desc The day the order was served on you
      `did I ask for a statement of reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you requested a statement of reasons for the decision under the Victorian Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 1998
      `have I been given reasons or told none will come` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been given the statement of reasons, or told under s 46(5) of that Act that none will be given
      `the day of the reasons or refusal` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the reasons or told none would be given (any date if not yet)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply to VCAT` MEANS
    `s 101(2) -- the last day` `the day it was served on me` `did I ask for a statement of reasons` `have I been given reasons or told none will come` `the day of the reasons or refusal`

-- "must be made within 28 days": after the last day, JUST FALSE (a period the text fixes). Reasons asked for and not yet
-- given or refused: JUST TRUE (the later day has not yet come).
@export Can I still apply to VCAT to review the interim prohibition order or prohibition order made against me (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) s 101)?
GIVEN `the day it was served on me` IS A DATE @desc The day the order was served on you
      `did I ask for a statement of reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you requested a statement of reasons under the Victorian Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 1998
      `have I been given reasons or told none will come` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been given the reasons, or told none will be given
      `the day of the reasons or refusal` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the reasons or told none would be given (any date if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you would apply
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still apply to VCAT` MEANS
    IF `did I ask for a statement of reasons` AND (NOT `have I been given reasons or told none will come`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `as an answer` (NOT (`today` `is after` (`s 101(2) -- the last day` `the day it was served on me` `did I ask for a statement of reasons` `have I been given reasons or told none will come` `the day of the reasons or refusal`)))

-- s 93 "A person who has been served with an interim prohibition order must comply with the order." s 98: the same for a
-- prohibition order. s 102 "A person must not provide a general health service in Victoria if, in another State or a
-- Territory ..., the person is prohibited from providing a service in the nature of that general health service." Each
-- 240 penalty units or 2 years or both (1200 for a body corporate). Prohibited: JUST FALSE ("must not"). Not prohibited:
-- the Act grants nothing (NOTHING-kind *silent*): other law may still apply.
@export May I provide this general health service in Victoria, given any prohibition order against me here or in another State or Territory (Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) ss 93, 98 and 102)? Not if an interim prohibition order or prohibition order served on you prohibits it, or if another State or Territory prohibits you from providing a service of that kind (up to 240 penalty units or 2 years' prison).
GIVEN `does a Victorian order served on me prohibit it now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an interim prohibition order or prohibition order served on you, and in force, prohibits you from providing this service (or the conditions it imposes are not met)
      `am I prohibited from it in another State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in another State or a Territory, you are prohibited from providing a service of this kind
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I provide this service in Victoria` MEANS
    IF `does a Victorian order served on me prohibit it now` OR `am I prohibited from it in another State or Territory`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

@export What is the most I can be fined for an offence under the Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic), in penalty units, as a provider? For example not responding to the Commissioner (ss 35, 52, 58), not producing documents (s 41), breaching a prohibition order (ss 93, 98) or an interstate prohibition (s 102). The dollar value of a penalty unit is set each year under the Monetary Units Act 2004.
GIVEN `which offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence, by section
      `am I a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a body corporate (answer no for an individual)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined` MEANS
    `the maximum penalty units for` `which offence` `am I a company`

@export What is the longest I can be imprisoned for an offence under the Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic), in months, as a provider? Only individuals: 12 months for not complying with an investigation hearing notice; 2 years for breaching an interim prohibition order, a prohibition order or an interstate prohibition; 0 where none.
GIVEN `which offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence, by section
      `am I a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a body corporate
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the longest I can be imprisoned` MEANS
    `the maximum months of imprisonment for` `which offence` `am I a company`
